{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoredox-mediated dearomative functionalization of electron-rich heteroarenes (thiophenes, furans, benzothiophenes, and indoles). By combining photoredox catalysis with hydrogen atom transfer (HAT), the authors achieved an umpolung strategy that generates electrophilic radical cations from electron-rich aromatics. This enables nucleophilic addition followed by a crucial HAT step to trap dearomatic radicals, preventing irreversible aromatization. Notably, the method discovered a noncanonical dearomative ring-cleavage of thiophenes and furans via C(sp2)-S/O bond breaking.",
